## 4. Group 3 — exact accepted forward composition

**Incoming source discharged literally.** The accepted published-chain proof assumes, over an algebraically closed characteristic-zero field, an actual polynomial Keller pair of degrees (75,125) that is already a standard (3,5) pair generating A0 = (5,20), A0' = (1,0), A1 = (7/5,2); its Fable gate restates the hypothesis as polynomial, standard (3,5), degrees 75/125, starting triple (5,20),(1,0),(5,-1), generated corner (7/5,2). Group 2 supplies exactly these over C: polynomial (phi in Aut(L)), standard, degrees 75/125, A0 and the type-II.b starting triple from Thm 2.20(13), A1 forced by the F2 row. The accepted gate's item (2) consumed a prior rectangle/pure-top normalization under the hypotheses "supports in {i+j <= 75, 5i-j <= 15}, {i+j <= 125, 5i-j <= 25}, nonzero corners"; these hold because (A0,(5,-1)) is a regular corner with en_(5,-1) = (15,60), (25,100) (v_(5,-1) = 15, 25 by Cor 5.7(2)-type proportionality), and in the present situation they are even automatic, since Prop 5.20's phi = id or y -> y + lambda keeps ML's rectangle. Bracket scalars: the accepted chain normalizes -T(Q1)/c and records the swap sign; only c0 != 0 is consumed. CONFIRMED.

